codex
The decoder serves only `rlwinm` and `rlwnm`; `rlwimi` has a separate arm and uses `arg[1]` as a destination pointer. The mask loop also leaves `mb == me`, so any repair must preserve the wrapping predicate before the loop.

I favor candidate (d): select dedicated wrapping handlers at decode time, retain the existing argument layout, and compile the added paths out under `MODE32`. This avoids relying on an unverified 64-bit argument slot.
codex
The arithmetic check passed all 1,024 mask pairs, all 32 shifts, and zero plus every single-bit source word against the manual’s 64-bit RTL. Correctly completed versions of all four candidates produce the right values; their differences are storage requirements and implementation risk.

Book I makes CR0’s comparison width depend on the current execution mode. `DOT0` passes the stored destination to `update_cr0`, but the helper’s implementation is outside the permitted files.
